      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HEARD OF HIM (4) was a rock solid $2.70 favourite first-up over 1250m at Newcastle and looked to have every chance but found a couple better. Improved to win second-up last prep over today's distance at Hawkesbury so the timing looks just right for this promising three-year-old. STAR HALF (2) won his maiden over 1250m at Newcastle two back then probably didn't appreciate going back in trip last time when well beaten here. Worth another chance at his first crack at 1400m. AUTUMN FLYER (3) settled back in the field and three-wide so his effort to get up for second recently over 1200m here was full of merit. Draws the fence and should relish getting out to 1400m for the first time. TIGER TURF (5) appreciated the drop in grade and collected his maiden win at Nowra last start. Harder this time - one for the exotics. The beautifully bred BARBAROSSA (1) is starting to put it together and from a better draw today can play a key role.",
